From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] alsa.conf: replace /usr/etc drop-ins with the three UAPI tiers
Source: Nex
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on a machine-generated transient tier

The installed src/conf/alsa.conf loaded distribution drop-ins from
/usr/etc/alsa/conf.d and fell back from /etc/asound.conf straight to
/usr/etc/asound.conf. /usr/etc is not a real search path on this
distribution, so both the drop-in directory and the single-file
fallback were silently unreadable.

Move the vendor drop-ins to /usr/share/alsa/conf.d, add a /run/alsa/conf.d
tier for transient, machine-generated fragments, and keep /etc/alsa/conf.d
as the administrator tier, loaded last so it overlays the other two. Give
the single-file fallback the matching order: /etc/asound.conf first, then
/run/asound.conf, then /usr/share/alsa/asound.conf as the packaged default.
/var/lib/alsa/conf.d (alsactl machine state), ~/.asoundrc,
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/alsa/asoundrc, and ALSA_CONFIG_PATH are unchanged.

diff -urN a/src/conf/alsa.conf b/src/conf/alsa.conf
--- a/src/conf/alsa.conf
+++ b/src/conf/alsa.conf
@@ -9,9 +9,10 @@
 		func load
 		files [
 			"/var/lib/alsa/conf.d"
-			"/usr/etc/alsa/conf.d"
+			"/usr/share/alsa/conf.d"
+			"/run/alsa/conf.d"
 			"/etc/alsa/conf.d"
-			"/etc/asound.conf|||/usr/etc/asound.conf"
+			"/etc/asound.conf|||/run/asound.conf|||/usr/share/alsa/asound.conf"
 			"~/.asoundrc"
 			{
 				@func concat
